# Frontend rendering of the "newsman_subscribe" content element.
#
# The plugin is rendered as EXTBASEPLUGIN instead of the
# `=< lib.contentElement` + `20 = EXTBASEPLUGIN` pair that
# ExtensionUtility::configurePlugin() generates. That pair only works when
# lib.contentElement is a COA: as soon as a site package redefines
# lib.contentElement as a FLUIDTEMPLATE, the numbered child is dropped and the
# element renders empty. Putting the object here instead also keeps it visible
# to site packages, which can override it.
#
# A site package that wants to put its own texts and design around the form
# overrides this object with a FLUIDTEMPLATE again, keeps the plugin as its
# child "20" and calls that child from its template with
# `<f:cObject typoscriptObjectPath="tt_content.{data.CType}.20" data="{data}"
# table="tt_content"/>`, the way the core does it in
# EXT:fluid_styled_content/Resources/Private/Templates/Generic.fluid.html. That
# way a newsletter block of the start page can look like the rest of the site.
#
# templateName is intentionally empty so Extbase resolves the template from the
# controller and action, which finds Resources/Private/Templates/Subscribe/
# Subscribe.html. A hard-coded name would break as soon as the file is renamed.
tt_content.newsman_subscribe = EXTBASEPLUGIN
tt_content.newsman_subscribe {
  extensionName = Newsman
  pluginName = Subscribe
  templateName =
}
